 > >
 > > The Convict is an escaped prisoner who seeks to redeem himself by
 > > seeking the Amulet in the Dungeons of Doom.  He starts out with a
 > > striped shirt, some rocks, and a heavy iron ball chained to him.  A
 > > trusty sewer rat accompanies the Convict into the dungeon: a companion
 > > from his days of imprisonment.
 > >
 > > Race: Human or Orc
 > > Alignment: Chaotic
 > > Deity: Tymora (Forgotten Realms)
 > >
 > > http://nethack.edeca.net/karl/nethack-convict-0.1.diff
 > >
 > >
 > >
 > >
 > > Spoiler Information:
 > >
 > > There may be a few surprises to this role for the unaware.  They start
 > > out with a small amount of bad luck, which times out, as well as a
 > > negative alignment ("You have transgressed").  This means that a
 > > Convict will not be able to pray successfully early on.  Some time and
 > > killing of monsters will make up for this before too long, though.
 > > They also start the game on the verge of hungry, which also makes the
 > > very early game challenging for Convicts.
 > >
 > > Stats: Excellent CON, good STR, average DEX and INT, poor WIS and CHA.
 > >
 > > Intrinsics: Sick resistance at level 7 (due to exposure to unhealthy
 > > prison conditions, as well as bad food).
 > >
 > > Pet: The convict starts with a sewer rat, which quickly advances to a
 > > giant rat, and can eventually become an enormous rat, then a rodent of
 > > unusual size.
 > >
 > > Iron Ball: The Convict starts with a heavy iron ball chained to him,
 > > as
 > > if he had read a scroll of punishment.  Since he starts with no real
 > > weapons apart from his rocks, he may wish to wield it as a weapon.
 > > Convicts (and only Convicts) may advance heavy iron ball as a weapon
 > > skill up to Basic.  This improves his chance to hit, and prevents him
 > > from automatically falling down the stairs if one is chained to him,
 > > so
 > > long as he is currently wielding it.
 > >
 > > Striped Shirt: Shopkeepers who can see the Convict wearing his striped
 > > shirt will recognize the player as an escaped prisoner, and will ban
 > > him from the shop.  Even if he later hides the shirt, that shopkeeper
 > > will remember the player.
 > >
 > > Guards: Guards who see a Convict will recognize him from wanted
 > > posters, and immediately become hostile.
 > >
 > >
 > > Weapon Skills:
 > >
 > > Basic: mace, short sword, quarterstaff, heavy iron ball, two-weapon
 > > combat
 > >
 > > Skilled: dagger, dart, hammer, sling
 > >
 > > Expert: club, knife, pick-axe, unarmed combat
 > >
 > >
 > > Spellcasting Skills:
 > >
 > > Basic: Attack, Divination
 > > Skilled: Matter
 > > Expert: Escape
 > >
 > >
